    "methods_description": "Wireless subdural ECoG recordings were acquired using an inductively powered implant with uniform sampling rates across sessions. Data were recorded during multiple task conditions including rest, pressing, reaching, listening, and sensorimotor tasks (abbreviated as 'sep'). Recordings include physiological ECoG channels, trigger channels, and auxiliary channels, with electrode locations and coordinate systems documented in BIDS-compliant metadata files. Raw .bin recordings were converted to BIDS-iEEG format using a custom Python-based converter. This dataset was independently curated from in-house raw recordings; while a related version is available on OpenNeuro (ds006890), this represents a separate BIDS reorganization maintained independently.",
